WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.972
<v Examiner>Define drug misuse, and drug abuse, with an example of each.

2
00:00:04.972 --> 00:00:06.338
<v Examiner>How are they different?

3
00:00:06.788 --> 00:00:09.095
The hook: misuse is the wrong purpose.

4
00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:11.887
Abuse is too much, for too long, and it hurts.

5
00:00:12.337 --> 00:00:13.155
Drug misuse.

6
00:00:13.155 --> 00:00:17.044
The World Health Organization's definition, on her slide:

7
00:00:17.044 --> 00:00:23.183
the use of any substance for a purpose that is different from legal or medical guidelines.

8
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:26.457
And there's a second, legal meaning in Aotearoa.

9
00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:29.732
Under New Zealand law, misuse means any illegal,

10
00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:35.530
harmful or unauthorised use of a controlled drug, under the Misuse of Drugs Act 1975.

11
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.896
Example: taking a medicine that was prescribed for someone else.

12
00:00:39.896 --> 00:00:45.148
Or taking your own prescribed medicine for a reason it wasn't prescribed for,

13
00:00:45.148 --> 00:00:46.308
like to get high.

14
00:00:47.758 --> 00:00:48.483
Drug abuse.

15
00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:53.495
Self-administration of a drug or substance in chronically excessive amounts,

16
00:00:53.495 --> 00:00:58.968
in a way that differs from approved medical use or the usual social patterns of the

17
00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:02.925
culture, and that results in physical or psychological harm.

18
00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:07.079
Three parts: chronically excessive, outside the norm, and harm.

19
00:01:07.079 --> 00:01:11.959
Example: drinking heavily every day, until it damages the person's health,

20
00:01:11.959 --> 00:01:13.409
work or relationships.

21
00:01:13.859 --> 00:01:14.837
The difference.

22
00:01:14.837 --> 00:01:18.550
Misuse is about the purpose being outside the guidelines.

23
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:22.394
Abuse adds the amount, chronically excessive, and the harm.

24
00:01:22.394 --> 00:01:28.062
And her notes add one thing: what counts as abuse is defined by what a society accepts,

25
00:01:28.062 --> 00:01:30.798
its own laws, history, religion and ethos.

26
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:31.880
<v Examiner>Once more.

27
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.955
<v Examiner>Misuse and abuse.

28
00:01:35.405 --> 00:01:41.076
Misuse: any substance used for a purpose different from legal or medical guidelines.

29
00:01:41.076 --> 00:01:43.237
In New Zealand law, any illegal,

30
00:01:43.237 --> 00:01:48.570
harmful or unauthorised use of a controlled drug under the Misuse of Drugs Act.

31
00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.934
Taking someone else's prescription.

32
00:01:50.934 --> 00:01:54.850
Abuse: self-administered in chronically excessive amounts,

33
00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:00.589
outside approved medical use or social norms, causing physical or psychological harm.

34
00:02:00.589 --> 00:02:03.829
Drinking heavily every day until it does damage.
